    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d510-a1">

                <pb facs="0841" n="705" xml:id="pg705"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 809.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sewall to Mr. Rives.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Apia, Samoa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 28, 1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 83.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith copy
                    of communication from the Imperial German consul in which he gives notice of the
                    immediate withdrawal of his Government from the municipality convention of 2d
                    September, 1879, prolonged by the protocol of 29th September, 1883.</p>
                <p>In this communication he also informs me that he is ready to enter into
                    negotiations with me and the British vice-consul respecting a division of the
                    property of the former municipality. I have acknowledged the receipt of this
                    communication and await the Department’s instructions.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harold Marsh Sewall</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
